cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use mmaemu, please cite it as below. Please also cite the tensor-core models it builds on:
  F. A. Khattak and M. Mikaitis, "Accurate Models of NVIDIA Tensor Cores", ACM Transactions on Architecture and
  Code Optimization 23(3), 2026, doi:10.1145/3830409 (arXiv:2512.07004).
type: software
title: "mmaemu: bit-accurate emulation of NVIDIA tensor-core FP8 GEMM numerics"
abstract: >-
  mmaemu reproduces, bit for bit, the FP8 GEMM numerics of a reference GPU (block accumulation, split-K
  reductions and the epilogue of cuBLAS FP8 GEMMs as called by torch._scaled_mm), so that results computed
  with the reference GPU's FP8 tensor cores can be recomputed on other devices. Version 0.1 models one
  reference platform (RTX 4060, sm_89, cuBLASLt 12.8.3.14) and is validated against hardware recordings of
  that GPU.
